Pure rename + one generalization, no behaviour change (the whole holo3
suite is green at this commit, and test_h3_plugins_tiles /
test_h3_tile_assembly / test_h3_schedule pass unchanged).

- `_tile_candidates`, `_attempt_many`, `_uncertified_streams` and
  `_union_reads` lose their underscore. A second tile row living in its
  own module (the 1000-line cap is a seam signal, tiles.py is at 808)
  must reach the same candidate gathering, the same attempt loop, the
  same uncertified-stream test and — critically — the SAME `reads`
  function object, because holo3/schedule.py derives the SCHEDULE.md
  reads column by AST-walking the module that defines `descriptor.reads`.
  A delegating copy in another module would render an empty column.
- `STAGE_POOL` + `HEAVY_STAGES`: `max_iters_for` now asks whether the
  stage is heavy rather than whether it is literally retry150. The
  pinned golden (scan, union, retry150) -> (60, 60, 150) is unmoved;
  no existing attempt key changes, because the new stage names nothing
  that ran before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
