From 9fd663921fb349820dd554b3ee15f69e9ef6d7f8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Germano Caronni <gec@acm.org>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 20:59:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] tiles.pool tests: the existence proof, the pairing pins,
 and the null proof
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

EXISTENCE PROOF (test_h3_plugins_pool.py, the row's reason to exist).
Two captures, two overlapping windows each, one independent noise draw
per window (seeded) on the same printed field of a real c3-k-r0550 tile,
amplitude 1.3 against sd 2.0. Measured through the real store and the
real codec at bp150: capture X alone FAILS, capture Y alone FAILS, the
winner-take-all union of both FAILS, the pooled assembly CERTIFIES — and
the certificate's user bits equal the printed bits, so zero-wrong holds
through an unchanged codec gate. The amplitude sits inside a measured
window (scratch sweep: pool closes from 1.2, union only from 1.6, a
single view only from 2.4), so the pin is not balanced on an edge.

BELOW-FLOOR NO LONGER ARMS, and the row loses nothing by it — pinned
with its proof: the pooled cut covers exactly the cells the union cut
covers (both are the union of every contributing window's cells), and
averaging can only send a cell to zero, never wake a silent one. A
below-floor verdict is therefore coverage-determined and pooling cannot
lift it; the tile still reaches the row through its union attempt's own
failure. This is what keeps the row off a whole sheet's worth of early
below-floor scans.

PAIRING: single-capture tiles mint nothing; two distinct captures at one
EXACT rational rung mint the union row's own subject and nothing else
(asserted equal to `tiles._union_subjects`, not merely similar); a
near-equal Fraction pairs nothing; two lanes of ONE capture never pool
with each other; a rung only one capture reaches mints nothing.

REFUSAL: with one window per capture the pooled cut is asserted
BIT-IDENTICAL to `assemble_union`'s (same bytes, same order, same
capture order) and prepare returns None — identical inputs never re-run.

MATHS: mean(+3, -1) = +1 within a capture (never the winner's +3, never
the sum +2), then +5 from the second capture sums to +6. Repeated
assembly is byte-identical; assembly writes nothing to the store
(store-snapshot diff empty).

PRICING: (110, 110, 220, 330) by fire ordinal; the engine's source
contains neither the number nor the stage name.

NULL PROOF: `pool_subjects` joins the decode record, and three sims
assert the row never births — the K sim, the colour sim, and the
degraded K capture, which leaves a real residue (6 failed attempts, 23
below the floor) and still mints nothing because one capture cannot
reach the pairing gate.

Gates at this commit, same machine: fast lane 1424 passed / 379 skipped;
slow lane (HOLO3_RUN_SLOW_TESTS=1) 1799 passed / 4 skipped, with every
pre-existing golden unmoved — the sims' byte-exact payloads, certificate
sets, mixed-sim union census and all three job-count churn tripwires,
which were frozen against the tree before this row existed and are
therefore the byte-identity evidence.

