From 343bd042bdeb3b991245b818379c66263b9f63a9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Germano Caronni <gec@acm.org>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 21:31:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] tiles.pool: the two-capture residue sim, and the measured
 reason no sim fires the row
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A second degraded capture — the same page, the same degradation, a
different noise draw — gives the tree its one sim whose residue SURVIVES
the run with two captures on it (status not-verified, 4 of 49 certified),
the closest analogue available to the real-sheet stack. On it the row
births three subjects, all inside `failed & union-covered`, and fires
zero times: that capture's surviving region is narrower than one window,
so every cell has exactly one reading per capture, the pooled cut IS the
winner-take-all cut, and the row declines to repeat an attempt already
made. Both facts are pinned.

AND THE NEGATIVE, recorded in the module docstring so the next reader
does not repeat the search: no sim in this tree fires the row end to
end, measured rather than assumed. Whole-page Gaussian degradation was
swept at sd 44, 48, 52, 56 and a banded one — heavy noise on two
interior tile rows, clean elsewhere, so placement stays healthy and the
damage is tile-local, the shape e029 measured as HP weak horizontal
lines — at sd 70, 85, 100. Every single one still certified 49/49 from
the scan stage alone. The sim's failure mode is all-or-nothing; the
residue this row exists for is the local, print-frozen kind. That is why
the yield case is the seven-capture sheet-H stack and not a sim.

Also pinned: the pooled job is a pure function of the store at fire time
(same store, byte-identical facts twice over), which is the property
that makes the worker count irrelevant to the commutative merge.

`_degraded_raster` takes its seed as an argument; the default is the
frozen one, so the existing single degraded capture is byte-identical.

Gates at this commit: fast lane 1428 passed / 383 skipped; slow lane
1807 passed / 4 skipped, every pre-existing golden unmoved; pyflakes
clean over holo3.

