Subject: [PATCH 6/6] tiles.pool: the discarded readings counted, not assumed

The module claimed windows overlap "by construction" and left the size
of the discard to the reader. Measured on the mixed sim instead: with
`window_starts(448)` = (0, 160, 248), of 138 tile-by-lane cover entries
30 are covered by one window and 108 by between two and nine. So on the
common tile the winner-take-all cut is throwing away most of the
readings the capture holds, which is the quantitative reason this row
exists rather than a plausible one.

